  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Settle a batch of trades as ONE aggregate reserve delta, so per-trade size\\nand direction are not derivable from chain data.\\n\\nv2 (2026-08-30) closes the last per-trade channel: the v1 circuits\\npublished `inputTotal`/`fee` per intent and `outAsset` per leg, and those\\npublics ride in THIS call's argument vectors \\xe2\\x80\\x94 so every leg's size and\\ndirection sat in the transaction envelope even though the event and the\\nreserves hid them. The v2 vectors carry commitments, nullifiers, the root\\nand the price alone; the fee arrives once as the aggregate's proven\\n`batchFee` ([10]).\\n\\nTHREE PROOFS PER BATCH-PLUS-TWO-PER-LEG, and each is load-bearing:\\n\\nintent (per leg) \\xe2\\x80\\x94 the notes exist, are unspent, and are bound to a\\nhidden trade. Intents never reach the chain, so without this the\\ncontract would be trusting the batcher that the inputs are real.\\nleg (per leg) \\xe2\\x80\\x94 the output note matches the batch's clearing price.\\naggregate (once) \\xe2\\x80\\x94 the published net flow really is the sum of the\\ncommitted amounts. The contract CANNOT deriv",
      "name": "batch_settle",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "relayer",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "legs",
          "type_": {
            "vec": {
              "element_type": {
                "udt": {
                  "name": "BatchLegInput"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "agg_proof",
          "type_": {
            "udt": {
              "name": "VProof"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "agg_inputs",
          "type_": {
            "vec": {
              "element_type": {
                "bytes_n": {
                  "n": 32
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "clearing_price",
          "type_": "i128"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "payloads",
          "type_": {
            "vec": {
              "element_type": "bytes"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        "u32"
      ]
    }
